# Networking

## Calls

- Declare Retrofit services in `data/remote/api/<Domain>Api.kt`; only repositories call them.
- Inject `SafeApiCall` into repositories as `safeApiCall` and wrap every call: `safeApiCall { api.foo() }` returns `ApiResult<T>`.
- Map to domain inside the repository (`.map { it.toDomain() }`); never return DTOs or throw from a repository.
- Never catch `CancellationException`; `safeApiCall` rethrows it.
- Express failures only through `AppError` (`NoInternet`, `Timeout`, `ServiceUnavailable`, `SessionExpired`, `Forbidden`, `NotFound`, `Validation`, `Server`, `Unknown`); changing it needs an impact analysis.
- Take base URL, timeouts and log level from `BuildConfig` (fed by `config/env/*.properties`); never hardcode URLs.

## DTOs and mappers

- DTOs live in `data/remote/dto`, are `@Serializable` (kotlinx.serialization) and never leave the `data` layer.
- Map with `toDomain()` extension functions in `data/mapper`.

## Auth

- Mark unauthenticated endpoints with `@Headers("$NO_AUTH_HEADER: true")`; `AuthInterceptor` strips the header and skips the token.
- Never add `Authorization` headers by hand; `AuthInterceptor` and `TokenAuthenticator` own them.
- Access tokens only through `TokenStore`; end sessions only through `SessionManager.endSession()`.

## Logging and secrets

- Never log tokens, `Authorization` or cookie headers, full request bodies outside `dev`, or personal data.
- Never read or print `local.properties`, `google-services.json`, keystores or `.env` files.

## Contracts and docs

- Register every new or changed endpoint in `../resturant-app-architecture/docs/03-context/API-REGISTRY.md` as `api:{domain}:{slug}` in the same change.
- Do not invent contracts: if the backend contract is unknown, add a PDR to `../resturant-app-architecture/docs/03-context/PENDING-DECISIONS.md` and stop.
- API contract or DTO changes trigger an impact analysis first.
- Use the `add-api-endpoint` skill to add an endpoint.
